#---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
1. Launch EC2 Instances for Control Plane and Worker Nodes[Created 1 control plane and 2 worker nodes]

2. To access the scripts run the following command
curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yogi0312/k8s/refs/heads/main/Cluster%20Setup/cluster_setup_using_kubeadm_1.36.sh

3. To install master node run the following command
curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yogi0312/k8s/refs/heads/main/Cluster%20Setup/cluster_setup_using_kubeadm_1.36.sh | bash -s master

4. To join any number of worker nodes by running the following on each as root:
kubeadm join 172.31.34.17:6443 --token d0rf5d.jkqmgjf8p345v9vx \
        --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:895c071b15f09fe348acf0ccf1a1d7af0e5b427638549777f5bafdd69dfa257a

5. To install worker node run the following command in both worker nodes[i.e. woker node1 nd worker node2 from AWS connect through SSH]
curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yogi0312/k8s/refs/heads/main/Cluster%20Setup/cluster_setup_using_kubeadm_1.36.sh | bash -s worker

6. In worker node 1 and worker node 2 run the following command to switch to root user
sudo su -

7. Allow incoming traffic to port 6443 in control-plane (master node) in AWS
SG ---> Inbound rules ---> Edit inbound rules ---> Add rule ---> Type: custom TCP, Port range: 6443, source: Anywhere-IPV4 ---> save rules

8. Run the folowing under root user in worker node 1 and worker node 2
kubeadm join 172.31.34.17:6443 --token d0rf5d.jkqmgjf8p345v9vx \
        --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:895c071b15f09fe348acf0ccf1a1d7af0e5b427638549777f5bafdd69dfa257a

9. Run 'kubectl get nodes' on the control-plane to see the worker node join the cluster.
